{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"],["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Design Principles","role":"article"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"]},{"title":"Explanation","generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class","text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"type":"text","text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" generates that class for you ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<StructName>Observer"},{"type":"text","text":") and wires up the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe"},{"type":"text","text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous","text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers take "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"type":"text","text":" and an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"type":"text","text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":". They never "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":", never "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"throw"},{"type":"text","text":", and never call I\/O directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back","text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" runs effects in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":" so they don’t block UI. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void"},{"type":"text","text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible","text":"4. Persistence is invisible","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers mutate "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" properties; "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" records every change in a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" debounces and drains those changesets through "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You never write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"type":"text","text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence","text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two structural patterns:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core middleware","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" for undo; ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keypaths for persistence)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain plugins","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The decision rule: "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"does this need to know your action type?"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" If no, write core middleware and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding(get:set:)"},{"type":"text","text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" and write back on a button."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", those plugins are blind to it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries","text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" snapshots in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so it must run "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drains changelogs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The recommended order:"}]},{"code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose","text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is built for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)"},{"type":"text","text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@concurrent"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async\/await"},{"type":"text","text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not","text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux gives you a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppEnvironment"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A network layer (use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"text":" and Swidux doesn’t care).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"11-Service-shapes-protocol-when-others-implement-it-closures-when-we-own-it","text":"11. Service shapes: protocol when others implement it, closures when we own it","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux services deliberately come in two shapes, chosen by who supplies the implementation:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Protocol"}]},{"text":" — when apps or vendor adapters implement the backend:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"text":" (RevenueCat, StoreKit, simulated), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Mixpanel, Amplitude, console), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsService"},{"text":" (any JSON host).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A protocol gives conformers a stable, documented contract.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Struct of closures"}]},{"text":" — when the library owns the shape and apps only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"configure or mock it: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchService"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalChallengeSource"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SyncPreflightService"},{"text":". Closures make the built-in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".live"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".mock"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factories and per-test overrides trivial without a conformance ceremony.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is a signal, not an accident: if you find yourself conforming to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"struct-of-closures service, that service was designed to be configured, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replaced."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Anti-patterns","text":"Anti-patterns","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"try","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Calling "},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from inside a reducer — use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Owning the store with "},{"code":"@StateObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — use "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"code":"ObservableObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Buffering form state in "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Registering "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" before "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — snapshot must precede mutation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}],"type":"topic","title":"StateWriter","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"type":"topic","title":"UndoPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"title":"Send","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","abstract":[{"text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Build Your First Swidux App","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Security Posture","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"title":"ChangeSet","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"title":"Swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Effect","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityStore","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","title":"binding(_:sending:)","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads a property through the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"binding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"KeyPath","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Observer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sending","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Binding","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SwiduxPlugin","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"}}}